{"created": "2023-05-25T15:39:42.439212+00:00", "modified": "2023-05-26T14:26:57.944673+00:00", "id": 7971310, "conceptrecid": "7971309", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7971310", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.7971309", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7971310", "metadata": {"title": "Energetic costs increase with faster heating in an aquatic ectotherm: Respirometry data", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7971310", "publication_date": "2023-05-25", "description": "<p>Using closed chamber respirometry we estimated the aerobic metabolic rate of an aquatic ectotherm, the Atlantic ditch shrimp <em>Palaemonetes varians,</em> under varying thermal conditions. We continuously measured oxygen consumption of shrimp during heating, cooling, and constant temperatures, starting trials at a range of acclimation temperatures and exposing shrimp to a variety of rates of temperature change.</p>\n\n<p>Data corrections and associated methodologies are detailed fully in the accompanying manuscript.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>## Description of the data and file structure</p>\n\n<p>Stable temperature trial data found in stable_trials_raw.csv</p>\n\n<p>Ramping temperature trial data found in ramping_trials_raw.csv</p>\n\n<p>Both datasets include the respirometry data for all temperature trials, with dissolved oxygen concentration corrected for background respiration (&quot;doconc_corr&quot;) following the methodology outlined in the associated manuscript. Identification number of the individual is stored under &quot;ID&quot;, time from start of trial to end of trial (in minutes) is stored under &quot;time_min&quot; and temperature of the chamber (in degrees Celcius) is stored under &quot;temp_degC&quot;.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Harding, Lucy", "affiliation": "Trinity College Dublin", "orcid": "0000-0003-2524-0492"}, {"name": "Jackson, Andrew L", "affiliation": "Trinity College Dublin", "orcid": "0000-0001-7334-0434"}, {"name": "Payne, Nicholas", "affiliation": "Trinity College Dublin", "orcid": "0000-0002-5274-471X"}], "keywords": ["temperature", "ectotherm", "climate change", "thermal ecology", "metabolism", "respirometry"], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "journal": {"title": "Conservation Physiology"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "18/SIRG/5549", "internal_id": "10.13039/501100001602::18/SIRG/5549", "funder": {"name": "Science Foundation Ireland", "doi": "10.13039/501100001602", "acronym": "SFI"}, "title": "Thermal scaling: rethinking how temperature drives macro-ecological patterns", "program": "SFI Starting Investigator Research Grant"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "7971309"}}]}}, "title": "Energetic costs increase with faster heating in an aquatic ectotherm: Respirometry data", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/7971310", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/7971310", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/7971310?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7971310", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7971310", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.7971310", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/7971310/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/7971309", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/7971309", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7971309", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.7971309", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:7971310/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:7971310/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/7971310/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/7971310/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/7971310/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/7971310/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/7971310/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/